1d","position":{"commit_sha":"da9a8e700c29b9d58941970a271ab898f2726507","position":"1786097265957002001-981ce511-7214-4916-a783-33e592a2e41d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"0301a61e8987e9f832aa10f260dff880a123e5d47991fbdba15656aad1c7edd4","event_uuid":"f0e33f99-bf13-4146-a464-42c287b409c2","position":{"commit_sha":"5acda6f78a92b5c61f2cf3710f5fede7c2b70e05","position":"1786098412362715001-f0e33f99-bf13-4146-a464-42c287b409c2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-224_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"71441096-fe6a-495c-aef3-76e194ce469c","close_class":"env_integration","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Fix pushed for review: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1478 (change 1478).\n\nThe guard now derives its candidate list from `git ls-files --cached --others --exclude-standard`\nwhen the root is a git repo — exactly 'tracked, plus untracked but not ignored' — so `.gitignore`\nis the single source of truth for scope and a brand-new file is still scanned the moment it is\nwritten. The `os.walk` denylist is kept verbatim as the fallback for a non-git root (the guard's\nown suite runs against throwaway tmp_path trees) and for a missing `git` binary.\n\nDeliberately did NOT just add `.claude/` and `bridge_state/` to EXCLUDED_DIRECTORY_NAMES: the\ndenylist-over-an-open-filesystem shape is the defect, and it would have drifted again.\n\nVerified against the polluted checkout that reproduces the bug (/Users/joeoakhart/rebar, which\nholds .claude/worktrees/ and bridge_state/): 47,312 violations before, 0 after, exit 0.\nConfirmed beforehand that all 47,312 were in gitignored paths and ZERO in git-tracked files, so\nno real violation is being suppressed.\n\nTests were RED before the fix (3 failures) and cover: a gitignored path is ignored; a tracked\nAND an untracked-but-unignored file still fail with the same path:line diagnostic; curated\nexclusions (docs/archive) and allowlist count pins still hold inside a git repo; and an absent\n`git` binary falls back to the walk.","timestamp":1786096016409570001}],"created_at":1786095474688828001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"af80983a-fa8c-4a18-8cdc-6f3496325989","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"a5f5-1059-cc11-4af6"},{"link_uuid":"3982bce2-584d-4c6f-96f2-8baa08548061","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"dbb2-5f6f-660d-4116"}],"description":"## The defect\n\n`scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py` — the deprecated-vocabulary guard wired into `make lint`\n— enumerates candidate files with a raw `os.walk` (`iter_repository_files`, ~line 144) filtered\nby a hand-maintained `EXCLUDED_DIRECTORY_NAMES` set (~line 23). That set covers `.git`, the\ntool caches, `.venv` and `node_modules`, but NOT `.claude/` or `bridge_state/`.\n\nBoth of those are gitignored (`.gitignore:49` and `.gitignore:14`) and both are created by\nnormal use of this repo: `make worktree` and the agent skills create `.claude/worktrees/<agent>/`,\nand the Jira bridge writes `bridge_state/snapshots/*.json`.\n\n## Measured in this checkout 2026-08-06\n\n    make lint  ->  47,312 \"deprecated vocabulary\" violations\n    violating files                       -> 1,393\n    of those that are git-tracked         -> 0\n\nEvery single violation is in a gitignored path — `.claude/worktrees/<agent>/docs/experiments/...`\n(an agent worktree carrying the repo's own frozen experiment corpora) and\n`bridge_state/snapshots/*.json`.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nCI never sees this because it does a fresh checkout with no worktrees and no bridge state. But\nthe pre-commit hook runs `make lint`, so any developer or agent who has ever created a worktree\nhas a permanently red commit gate for reasons unrelated to their change. The obvious escape is\n`git commit --no-verify`, which disables the whole gate — so a hand-maintained exclusion list\nthat drifts converts a quality gate into pressure to bypass quality gates.\n\nThe exclusion list is the root cause, not the two missing entries: it is a denylist over an\nopen-ended filesystem, so it will drift again the next time the repo grows a gitignored\ndirectory.\n\n## Approach\n\nDerive the candidate file list from git (`git ls-files --cached --others --exclude-standard`)\nso the guard considers exactly the files git would — tracked plus untracked-but-not-ignored —\nand `.gitignore` becomes the single source of truth for what is out of scope. Keep the existing\n`os.walk` as the fallback for a non-git-repo root (the guard's own tests run it against\nthrowaway `tmp_path` trees), and keep every existing curated exclusion (`docs/archive`,\n`docs/experiments`, the minified `editor.js`, symlinks) applied on top, so behaviour for\ntracked files is unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] A violating phrase in a gitignored path does not fail the guard.\n- [x] A violating phrase in a tracked (or untracked-but-not-ignored) file still fails the guard,\n      with the same path:line diagnostic as today.\n- [x] The guard still works when the root is not a git repository (its own test suite depends on\n      this), and does not crash when `git` is absent.\n- [x] The existing curated exclusions and the allowlist count-pin semantics are unchanged.\n- [x] A test proves the gitignored-path case, RED before the fix.\n- [x] `make lint` reports 0 vocabulary violations in a checkout that contains\n      `.claude/worktrees/` and `bridge_state/`.\n\n## Provenance\n\nFound while fixing bug a5f5 (`make worktree` builds its venv from ambient python3): creating a\nworktree is exactly the action that reproduces this.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py","reason":"derive the candidate file list from git ls-files so gitignored paths are out of scope; keep os.walk as the non-git fallback"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_check_criteria_vocabulary.py","reason":"RED-first contracts: gitignored paths ignored, tracked/unignored still caught, curated exclusions + allowlist counts unchanged, missing git falls back"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["relates_to","dbb2-5f6f-660d-4116"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"f0e33f99-bf13-4146-a464-42c287b409c2","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"d5ae-5f4a-858f-431b","ticket_type":"bug","title":"make lint is broken in any checkout with a worktree: the vocabulary guard walks gitignored paths","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["572b621b-e3e3-489b-9e55-2a8df93607a6","6561dac9-866e-40e8-af58-a0b1a4f97b09","7317474a-5fe9-491e-bd4a-0573b2e748a1","af80983a-fa8c-4a18-8cdc-6f3496325989","3982bce2-584d-4c6f-96f2-8baa08548061","a3c8bcf3-8d2b-42fb-9b07-a77b1e591b61","0dcbb05c-8a7b-422a-b8be-cb6ef9e9b92c","981ce511-7214-4916-a783-33e592a2e41d","f0e33f99-bf13-4146-a464-42c287b409c2"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786659676884219001,"uuid":"9a6b307e-7c85-4a43-a473-fad3792ca663"}